'''Osmumten''' was the last pharaoh of the line of pharaohs chosen by [[Tumeken]], the God of the Sun. Besides being ruler, Osmumten was a passionate hunter, wielding his [[Osmumten's fang|specially designed weapon]], he adventured across the land, fighting the greatest beasts. Osmumten was the pharaoh somewhere around the [[Second Age]], when the present-day [[Kharidian Desert]] was invaded by the [[Zarosian Empire]] in the [[Kharidian–Zarosian War]].

Osmumten was fighting on the frontline in the war, which ended when Tumeken sacrificed himself to stop the invading forces. Following Tumeken's supposed death, his widow [[Elidinis]], the Goddess of Fertility, gave Osmumten [[Tumeken's shadow]] and the [[Elidinis' ward]] before retreating to mourn her husband's death and the unfortunate fate of her daughter [[Amascut]].
[[File:Tombs of Amascut - Osmumten's burial chamber.png|thumb|left|250px|Osmumten's spirit in his burial chamber.]]
Osmumten would continue ruling as the last pharaoh appointed by Tumeken. However it was not long after the pyrrhic victory against the [[Zaros]]ians that Osmumten was blamed by a group of usurpers (the ancestors of the modern day [[Menaphite thug|Menaphite gang]]), who killed him and his entire family, save his son [[Mehhar]], who was saved by the family's servants and brought to [[Ullek]], where he would live with the Sect of [[Scabaras]].

His spirit can be found besides his sarcophagus inside the [[Tombs of Amascut]], commending the player on their apparent victory over Amascut after defeating the [[Warden]], but also warning that Amascut's forces will be back again and that the player's help is still needed.

